ason verbatim from `_try_create_github_issue` on the integer-ID path; beads and\n   unknown string-ID branches gain only `, None` and are otherwise untouched.**\n   Verified: `operations.py:1474-1509`.\n\n3. **`add_item` unpacks `(issue_ref, issue_error)` and conditionally sets\n   `result[\"error\"]` only when `issue_error` is truthy \u2014 omitted (not `None`) on\n   success and on the tolerated GitHub-unavailable fallback.**\n   Verified: `operations.py:1612` (unpack), `operations.py:1655-1657` (conditional set,\n   omit-on-success convention preserved).\n\n4. **CLI `backlog add` exits non-zero (code 1) when the result dict carries `error`,\n   after `_emit(result, output)` has already printed the JSON payload.**\n   Verified: `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py:76-78`, an exact\n   two-line diff matching the architect spec. Exercised live through Typer's real\n   `CliRunner` (not mocked at the dispatch layer \u2014 only `operations.add_item`'s return\n   value is mocked) in the new test\n   `test_add_exits_nonzero_when_result_carries_an_error_without_raising`\n   (`sam_schema/tests/test_backlog_cli.py:86-115`) \u2014 re-ran, 1 passed, confirms\n   `exit_code == 1` and the full JSON payload (including `error`) is preserved on\n   stdout.\n\n5. **GitHub-unavailable stays a silent, error-free local-only create (#2999 regression\n   guard) \u2014 this is a required negative truth, not just an omission.**\n   Verified: `test_add_item_item_ref_empty_when_no_github_issue` now asserts\n   `\"error\" not in result` in addition to `item_ref == \"\"`; re-ran, passed.\n   `test_add_item_local_only_pending_state_visible_via_list_and_view` is unmodified\n   (confirmed via diff read) and passes unmodified, proving the #2999 fallback survived\n   the tuple-widening untouched.\n\n6. **New test covers the reported-failure branch the item exists to fix.**\n   `test_add_item_error_set_when_issue_creation_raises`\n   (`tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py:437-454`) m